<% if @credentials_deleted %>
You deleted all keys, tokens, and their associated SSO authorizations for @<%= @target_user.display_login %> in <%= @enterprise_name %>

You deleted all user keys, tokens, and their associated SSO authorizations for @<%= @target_user.display_login %> in <%= @enterprise_name %>.
<% else %>
You revoked all SSO authorizations for keys and tokens belonging to @<%= @target_user.display_login %> in <%= @enterprise_name %>

You revoked all SSO authorizations for keys and tokens belonging to @<%= @target_user.display_login %> that have access to <%= @enterprise_name %>.
<% end %>
<% if @revoked_counts.values.any? { |v| v > 0 } %>

<% if @revoked_counts[:classic_pats].to_i > 0 %>
- <%= pluralize(@revoked_counts[:classic_pats], "personal access token") %> (classic)
<% end %>
<% if @revoked_counts[:fine_grained_pats].to_i > 0 %>
- <%= pluralize(@revoked_counts[:fine_grained_pats], "fine-grained personal access token") %>
<% end %>
<% if @revoked_counts[:oauth_app_tokens].to_i > 0 %>
- <%= pluralize(@revoked_counts[:oauth_app_tokens], "GitHub App and OAuth app user access token") %>
<% end %>
<% if @revoked_counts[:ssh_keys].to_i > 0 %>
- <%= pluralize(@revoked_counts[:ssh_keys], "SSH key") %>
<% end %>
<% end %>
<% if @credentials_deleted %>

This was a permanent action. The user will need to generate new tokens, SSH keys, SSO authorizations, and organization access granted by fine-grained personal access tokens before they can access enterprise resources again.
<% else %>

This affected all of the user's SSH keys and tokens that had access to organization-level resources where SSO was enforced. This was a permanent action, and the affected tokens and keys cannot be reauthorized.
<% end %>

You can review the full list of affected credentials in your enterprise audit log: <%= @audit_log_url %>

If you did not perform this action, please contact GitHub Support immediately.
